Subject: [PATCH 02644/11362] [outer-loop] Config Layer B rewrite digest: tr87
 glyph-substitution from pixels -- segmentation solved, cross-region
 glyph-value matching is the gap

Operator directive: build the rewrite-class digest and re-test tr87. Reframing established: tr87's
mechanic is KNOWN (glyph substitution, RE'd by the adapter), so its Layer-B verifier is a deterministic
from-pixels glyph-decode, NOT an LLM induction (induction is for UNKNOWN mechanics like ka59). This is
the pixel-perception upgrade the original solve deferred (it read internal state).

Fully RE'd tr87 pixel structure: glyph value = the 5-on bitmap (frame-agnostic); A-series (target + rule
LHS) are colour-10-framed, B-series (editable + rule RHS) are colour-7-framed; 3 rule bands = 6 (A->B)
pairs; win = editable_B == [map[a] for a in target_A].

Built a reusable glyph-segmentation primitive (split a sprite band into 5x5 tiles by on-pixel column
gaps; value_id = on-pixel-bbox bitmap). It segments EVERY region cleanly (editable/target/3 rule bands
-> w=5 tiles) and decodes the 6 rules; editable B-glyphs match rule RHS 3/5. GAP: target A-glyphs match
rule LHS only 1/5 -- the same value renders to slightly different bitmaps across regions (18 ids for ~7
values), so exact-bitmap clustering over-splits. Honest boundary: segmentation solved; cross-region
glyph-value identity needs a TOLERANT matcher (Hamming-nearest or a 7-way classifier), not exact equality.
verdict complete_glyph_pixel_decode_partial_not_grounded. Adversarial-verify clean.

